WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:03.020
Hello! This is "Hayate No Gotoku!"

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.650
The last episode ended with 
a bombshell revelation!

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.540
Could it be a trap?

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:12.230
<i>I love all kinds of liquor, but sweet sake is the best.</i>

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.360
Who is this mysterious beauty?

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.780
Night two is full of mystery.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.050
I'm sure it'll be quite exciting!

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:14.790
<i>Sweet sake is delicious.</i>

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:16.950
Also, we'll finally unveil the opening sequence

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:20.080
<i>Sweet sake is even good frozen.</i>

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.760
we've worked so hard on!

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:21.530
You can treasure each frame.

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:25.170
Now, please enjoy night two of "Hayate No Gotoku!"

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.190
<i>Ayasaki-kun, Ayasaki-kun. Want some sweet sake?</i>

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.190
Um... No.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.340
Too bad!

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.510
It's all gone, anyway!

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.460
Actually, teacher,

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.250
I think there's still some 
sweet sake over there.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.210
What, really? Yay!

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:40.690
We got her?

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:41.950
Yeah, we did.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.370
Katsura-chan.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.050
Let's bury her a bit more.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:45.910
<i>Good idea.</i>

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:46.980
Let's start the show!

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:50.550
I'm...

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.900
I'm Ruri Tsugumi.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:55.350
I'm Nagi Sanzenin's

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:57.660
little sister!

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.810
Hey! Why did you close the door?

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:07.220
<i>At least listen to me!</i>

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:12.000
<i>Hey! Hey, I said! Hey! Come on!</i>

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:09.420
What's going on?

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.340
Not sure...

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:00.820
Hey, Hayate!

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.260
Some weirdo's at the door!

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.290
Huh? Pardon?

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:08.390
A weirdo?

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:10.160
Whoa! You're still here?

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.690
Friend of yours?

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.580
Um... Well...

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:18.820
<i>I... I'm... Nagi Sanzenin's...</i>

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:18.820
She claims she's your little sister

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:20.870
and followed us home last night.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.050
Little sister?

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:24.150
I was my mom's only child.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.600
Then she must be your half sister.

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:28.730
Half sister?

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:31.850
Do we really need a back 
story like that now?

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:34.680
Saying that to me won't...

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:34.640
<i>Um... I'm...</i>

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.710
And if we have to do a back story,

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:38.930
wouldn't making her <i>your</i>
 sister be a better twist?

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:41.860
Like, have 12 girls show up 
calling you "Big Brother"!

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:44.720
No one would buy that storyline now.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.440
People will wonder how many 
years ago this happened!

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.870
It's as impossible as a 
Buddha getting angry.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:51.960
Well, anyway.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.740
She says she's my sister, but...

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:56.130
Let's just have breakfast for now.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:03:59.420
Sure.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:01.130
We have egg muffin sandwiches.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.490
W-Wait a second...

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.340
Um... I...

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:20.230
Oh? You're still...

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:26.780
Um... Would you mind... 
listening for just a bit...

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:28.220
Huh?

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:32.870
Listen, you can't be 
mean to little girls.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.150
No, you can't!

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:38.000
<b> (CAGRI)ostro no... Shiro (LOL)</b>

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:40.550
So, what does my self-professed little sister,

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:43.130
the Currently Assumed Generic 
Relationship Indicator, want?

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.250
I'm not your "self-professed" 
sister! I'm actually her!

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:46.760
What's all that "Currently Assumed" stuff?

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.390
<b> (LOL)</b>

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:48.390
Then, "little sister (LOL)."

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.150
That's worse! I'm not a joke!

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.210
You make it sound like I'm stupid!

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.660
You aren't?

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.980
Don't call me stupid!

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:58.460
So...

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:59.980
What's your agenda?

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:01.730
Huh? Agenda?

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:04.750
Yes, the reason you're here.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:05.860
You have one, right?

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.550
I... I'm here because...

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:09.990
We're family and I wanted to meet...

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:10.990
No.

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:13.930
I don't wanna hear excuses.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:17.170
You're here for a 
particular reason, right?

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:22.680
I don't need to keep 
hearing you're my sister.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.010
I believe you.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:27.880
But now what?

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.440
You're my sister. So what?

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:34.340
You're my sister. 
Now what do you want?

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:36.320
Um... Uh...

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:39.140
Take your time. Choose 
your words wisely.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:41.070
If you don't answer correctly...

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.820
Hayate will break your neck!

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.060
No!

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.280
I wouldn't do that.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.590
In any case, I don't have an agenda!

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.280
As your sister, I wanted to...

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:52.960
Oh, my sister.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:55.480
Do you have any proof 
that you're my sister?

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:59.830
Um... No... I never met my dad,

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:02.340
and I don't have any photos...

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:04.240
And my mom died...

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:05.340
Mother?

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.430
Who's your mother? Where was she from?

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.800
Um... Well...

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.280
I don't have any other relatives,

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:16.180
but then I found out about you...

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:20.810
I really just wanted to 
meet my family and...

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:23.570
It's out of love! Only love!

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.830
Hm. I see.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:34.700
Huh?

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:36.910
Do you have a place to stay?

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:38.470
No, I don't.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:39.960
Then I'll prepare one for you.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.000
Really?

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.310
Wait for me in the hall.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:44.350
Okay, I'll wait. I'll wait!

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:52.870
Based on her behavior,

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.740
I don't think she's your sister.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:56.220
Well, I'm not too sure.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:01.730
After talking with her, there's about 
a 3% chance she is my sister.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:02.720
Huh?

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:05.420
Yeah, about 3%.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:09.670
I've never met him, but it's 
possible that my stupid father

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:12.990
had an affair before he died that

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.660
resulted in a child...

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.060
Do you know something that'd

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.370
make that scenario likely?

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:21.920
Well, maybe.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:23.830
Huh?

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:27.390
So are we letting her 
stay in the mansion?

00:07:27.390 --> 00:07:29.280
Yes. Because...

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:42.480
Ruri Tsugumi.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:45.360
Hey!

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:49.590
You came to me claiming to be my sister

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:51.170
so you'd be accepted here

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:54.010
and get a chance to look for 
something in the mansion, right?

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:56.620
N-No! It's not like that!

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:57.760
Don't lie.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:02.000
You looked quite relieved 
when I said you could stay.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:07.590
But I never go back on my word, 
so I have a room for you.

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:11.740
The perfect room for someone like you...

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:21.470
<i>Amaaaaazing</i>

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:23.940
<i>Graaaaace...</i>

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:27.030
<i>How...</i>

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:34.610
<i>Amaaaaazing</i>

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:36.180
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:37.650
<i>Graaaaaace...!</i>

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:45.230
What did you do that for all of a sudden?!

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:47.130
That's my line!

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:50.460
What's with the crazed,
 half-assed singing?

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.510
Does it matter?

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.660
Yes, it does!

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:56.460
Think of how bummed the
 drawing staff must be!

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:58.480
What're you talking about?

00:08:58.480 --> 00:08:59.720
Hey, now.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:03.590
I was getting a good laugh out 
of her comic musical number.

00:09:03.590 --> 00:09:04.730
Don't stop her!

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:06.980
A good laugh?!

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:09.730
It wasn't meant to be funny.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:13.160
Anyway, I brought over a new tenant.

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:19.280
A new tenant?

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:20.700
And who is this?

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:24.710
My little sister (currently assumed), 
Ruri Tsugumi.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:25.710
Sister?

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:27.460
You have a sister, Nagi-chan?

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.580
Yeah. She buzzed over this morning.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:32.960
Sisters don't swarm like 
mosquitoes, do they?

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.470
Who're you calling a mosquito?!

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:36.360
So that's about it.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:37.900
Have a good life, now.

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:40.130
You take care of the rest, Hayate.

00:09:40.130 --> 00:09:40.800
Uh-huh.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.720
What? No, wait a sec!

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.940
You're just leaving the 
rest to him? That's it?

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.090
Yeah, that's it.

00:09:49.090 --> 00:09:54.030
I couldn't care less if 
you're my sister or not.

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:55.430
You take care.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:55.990
<i>W-Wait.</i>

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:57.740
Big sister!

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:06.960
What... was that?

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:11.080
Please! I want you to 
hear me out, big sister.

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:13.210
B-Big sister?

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:17.220
Yes. You're my big sister, so...

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:21.780
I'm not going to be 
swayed by endearments!

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:25.140
Hey, wait! Big sister!

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:30.710
<b>Connecting</b>

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:30.710
<b>Theater</b>

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:30.710
<b>Part A</b>

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:34.740
Sharna-chan. Sharna-chan. 
Fumi is growing up.

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:38.390
I'd like to get dressed up
 and stroll around town.

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:40.080
Yes, Fumi-chan.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:42.490
Technically, you are a girl, Fumi-chan.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:45.590
How do you want to dress?

00:10:45.590 --> 00:10:47.250
What sort of look?

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:49.890
Oh, uh... I'm thinking

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:52.500
I'd like to look like the 
chief cabinet secretary.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:55.310
That will be a steep hill to climb.

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:55.960
<i>Oh, a butterfly!</i>

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:01.660
<b>Connecting</b>

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:01.660
<b>Theater</b>

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:01.660
<b>Part B</b>

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:03.610
Sharna-chan, Sharna-chan.

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:05.570
Fumi is growing up.

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:07.710
I would like to get a cute pet.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:10.440
Yes, pets are cute.

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:14.190
What kind of pets have
 you had in the past?

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:15.570
A custard roll.

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:18.350
I see. It must have been cute.

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:21.700
Oh, a Countach!

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:31.210
Time is cruel.

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:34.310
Your face, your voice...

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:38.020
become sand and spill from my hands.

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:41.220
Pitifully fragile,

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:43.760
and sadly fickle.

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:47.260
But I will continue to search

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:49.720
for that which was lost beyond time.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.060
I will wander forever...

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:53.520
I will continue my search.

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:58.060
As long as I hold this last grain of sand.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.230
Ah. Where are you now?

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:25.060
<i>Do you have proof that 
you're my sister?</i>

00:12:25.730 --> 00:12:28.500
<i>I never met my dad,</i>

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:30.490
<i>and I don't have any photos...</i>

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:41.220
<i>Not even one...</i>

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:46.700
Wait! Wait for me, big sister!

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:47.870
Let me go!

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.610
You have no business 
calling me "big sister"!

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:53.350
<i>Don't be like that, big sister!</i>

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:51.990
Is this okay?

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:55.710
Well, she certainly doesn't look dangerous.

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:56.130
<i>Ugh! Let me go!</i>

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:58.470
This explains the saying: 
"There's no battle unless

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:00.710
both parties are on the same level."

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.510
What?

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:04.840
Hello, Kayura-san!

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:06.540
Yes, hello.

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:09.510
You've really grown 
quite weak, Nagi.

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:10.510
What?

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:14.730
One day, without any warning, 
your stepsister appears.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:20.520
But all you do is fight against this 
delicious new development!

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:23.810
And you call yourself an 
aspiring manga artist

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:26.430
who aims to sell one 
trillion comic books?!

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:28.080
I can't believe you're not taking full

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:30.030
advantage of this wildly 
interesting twist!

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:37.410
She always has such silly reasoning.

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:38.380
Uh, yeah.

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:41.200
I see!

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:42.630
You're absolutely correct.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.710
She's accepted it.

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.970
Manga maniacs think so differently.

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:50.850
Okay, I get it. I'll give you a chance.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.080
A chance?

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:52.850
Right.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:55.560
If you claim to be my sister,

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:57.600
you must have some skill.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:59.520
If not, you're in deep trouble.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:02.440
For example, I, Nagi Sanzenin,

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:06.570
possess tremendous skills that 
make me the perfect superhuman!

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:09.620
A perfect superhuman who 
can't handle basic skills

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.330
like sleeping and waking early.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:14.080
A perfect superhuman 
who's not very athletic.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.830
Everyone shut up!

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:19.590
So if you claim to be 
my sister, then you'd

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:21.590
better show me some crazy skill.

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:26.030
If you do, then I might be 
somewhat interested in you.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:30.090
O-Okay.

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:35.180
I, Ruri Tsugumi, will accept 
my sister's challenge!

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:44.240
So, what can you do, Tsugumi-san?

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.240
Well...

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:51.610
Oh! I know what I'm good at!

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:53.370
Oh? What is it?

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.870
Systema!

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:55.740
Huh?

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:56.790
Systema?

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:57.670
What?

00:14:57.670 --> 00:14:59.290
S-Systema?

00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:00.330
Yes!

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:02.670
What's that?

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:05.380
Listen, Systema is...

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:08.220
A type of martial art invented

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:10.430
by the Russian Special Forces 
for close quarter combat.

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:14.560
Today, it's considered the most 
intense martial art in history!

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:24.970
Really?

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:26.200
Is that right?

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:28.650
But you were yelling 
like crazy yesterday...

00:15:29.710 --> 00:15:31.720
Anyone taken for a ride like that

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:34.640
would be scared, even if 
you're a Systema master!

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:37.510
Even a mammoth would 
be reduced to tears!

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.910
Well, I suppose so.

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:45.380
But can you really do Systema?

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:53.930
What just happened?

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:58.050
That was Systema. The hand-to-hand,

00:15:58.050 --> 00:16:01.640
close combat martial art of modern warfare!

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:03.290
W-Wow!

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:05.560
You were so flexible and nimble!

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.520
Make no mistake, that was Systema!

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:09.900
You guys know a lot about this.

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:13.910
But he wasn't paying attention. Hayate!

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:14.910
Y-Yes!

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:21.210
I bet you don't know 
what just happened.

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:24.310
Oh no, Ayasaki-kun!

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:26.170
Don't let her land a hit to your chest!

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:34.590
<i>How strange. The attacks 
don't feel that strong, but...</i>

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:40.100
<i>I... can't... stand...</i>

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:41.350
Hayate-kun!

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:42.350
What the?

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:45.500
Ayasaki-kun went down 
as easily as a child.

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:49.150
How's that possible when 
he's so much bigger?

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:50.730
It's how she attacked.

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:52.110
How she attacked?

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:55.280
Systema is called Russia's Aikidou.

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:56.700
By evading the attack

00:16:56.700 --> 00:17:01.250
and changing direction, 
you can deal massive damage.

00:17:01.860 --> 00:17:02.790
As demonstrated,

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:05.750
if you attack by throwing 
your energy downward,

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:08.260
you can upset your opponent's balance.

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:09.760
I see.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:17.510
Commentary                        Play-By-Play

00:17:10.010 --> 00:17:12.610
But even if you understand the moves,

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:15.160
you have to practice 
hard to make them work.

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:17.510
You're in a spot, Ayasaki-kun.

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:21.770
You sound like a commentator 
in a martial arts manga.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:25.790
I get it. I get it, Tsugumi-san.

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:28.770
I understand you have an 
incredible skill. So please...

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:31.780
Are you going to tell me you give up?

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:32.820
Huh?

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.780
After what I endured on the bike...

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:40.200
I must take revenge for yesterday's 
embarrassment right now!

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:46.320
<i>Her attacks aren't strong,</i>

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:48.040
<i>but the pain reaches my bones...</i>

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:50.300
That's also a Systema move!

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:52.800
Damage is felt directly by his bones!

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:57.640
It's as the commentator says.

00:17:57.640 --> 00:17:59.850
Those like you without
special training cannot

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:01.390
defend themselves against Systema!

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:02.810
I'm not done yet!

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:05.210
Hey... Let's stop this now.

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:07.440
You understand everything. 
Right, Miss Nagi?

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:09.100
What are you saying?

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:12.480
My Hayate shouldn't crumble under 
some Russian martial arts move!

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:15.440
Go Hayate! Die before you lose!

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:21.470
<i>Oh... I haven't felt 
like this in a while...</i>

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:25.370
<i>It's the same feeling as before...</i>

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:30.540
Dance! Dance until your feet 
don't touch the ground!

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:37.760
I will never forget the shame 
you put me through!

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:39.890
Die!

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:43.390
<i>Shoot! If this keeps up, 
I'll really...</i>

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:53.710
Stop! Hayate-kun will die!

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:59.990
Commentary                        Play-By-Play

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:56.000
Oh no! We'll also...

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:58.110
...keep morphing more and more into

00:18:58.110 --> 00:18:59.990
martial arts manga commentators!

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:03.290
<i>Shoot.</i>

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:05.630
<i>I have no choice. If she's going 
to keep coming at me</i>

00:19:05.630 --> 00:19:07.120
<i>with Russian martial arts...</i>

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:08.960
And here's the killer blow!

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.990
<i>I'm going to counter with</i>

00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:12.920
<i>an ancient Japanese martial arts move!</i>

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:14.170
Is it coming?

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:20.280
<i>Ketaguri</i>

00:19:17.650 --> 00:19:19.090
Ketaguri!

00:19:42.560 --> 00:19:44.950
Huh? Um, wait!

00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:49.060
That was too much, Hayate-kun.

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:50.530
You went too far.

00:19:50.530 --> 00:19:53.210
She's just a child.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:58.210
Huh? What? What?

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:00.010
Ow! It hurts!

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:02.970
Sorry! Are you hurt?

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:12.210
You're naive, Hayate Ayasaki!

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:14.760
Tricks are the norm in battle.

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:15.980
You relax and you lose!

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:19.260
How dare you do that to Hayate!

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:25.740
Ouch! Big sister!

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:29.240
Shut up! You're not my sister!

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:44.090
But you can live 
here for the time being.

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:44.840
Okay?

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:46.780
Big sister...

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:47.840
Shut up!

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:50.800
You're in no place to call me "big sister."

00:20:55.380 --> 00:20:58.900
Well... But... You know.

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:02.900
That Systema stuff is really cool.

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:05.840
Can you teach it to me sometime?

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:14.180
Y-Yes! Maybe I will teach you!

00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:19.550
Don't talk down to me, 
you idiot! Idiot!

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:21.610
Teach us too!

00:21:23.780 --> 00:21:28.910
 Ruri Tsugumi

00:22:59.070 --> 00:23:04.330
Did you enjoy night two 
of "Hayate No Gotoku!"?

00:23:02.090 --> 00:23:04.270
<i>What's happened to Katsura?</i>

00:23:04.270 --> 00:23:06.800
<i>She should have cooled down by now.</i>

00:23:04.330 --> 00:23:07.130
Wasn't Ruri Tsugumi strong?

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:09.340
She's a one-woman Systema machine!

00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:10.690
<i>She was in there throughout 
the commercial break.</i>

00:23:09.340 --> 00:23:12.060
But what is her agenda?

00:23:10.690 --> 00:23:13.410
<i>I hope she's straightened up a bit.</i>

00:23:12.060 --> 00:23:13.510
Intriguing, isn't it?

00:23:13.410 --> 00:23:14.730
<i>I doubt it.</i>

00:23:14.590 --> 00:23:17.430
And we'll have a new twist next week.

00:23:14.730 --> 00:23:15.690
<i>Never.</i>

00:23:15.690 --> 00:23:17.430
<i>Not happening.</i>

00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:21.000
That character you've all been 
waiting for will finally appear!

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:23.600
What sort of romance will develop?

00:23:21.340 --> 00:23:23.160
<i>Where's the sake?</i>

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:24.680
<i>Whoa!</i>

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:24.680
<i>-She's alive!</i>

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:24.680
<i>-Are you all right?</i>

00:23:23.600 --> 00:23:27.180
What awful things will happen to me next?

00:23:24.680 --> 00:23:27.330
<i>How dare you trick me, Ayasaki-kun!</i>

00:23:27.180 --> 00:23:28.460
Stay tuned!

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:30.050
<i>Caught!</i>

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:31.270
<i>Caught again!</i>

00:23:31.770 --> 00:23:34.720
Let's pack the snow down, this time.

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:35.690
Okay!

00:23:35.690 --> 00:23:36.830
Got it.

00:23:36.830 --> 00:23:38.220
Look forward to it!

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:38.220
<i>Let's do this!</i>

00:23:38.220 --> 00:23:38.890
Yay!
